From: PS3 Custom Toolchain
Subject: [PATCH] rs6000: canonicalize hybrid relative tablejump targets

The Cell ELF64/ILP32 ABI has TARGET_64BIT with Pmode == SImode.
Relative tablejump expansion therefore skips the DI sign extension and
adds a zero-extended 32-bit table word to its base with a physical 64-bit
add. A negative displacement can leave bit 32 set before mtctr/bctr.

Canonicalize the completed SI target through the existing patch-0032
ps3_ptr_canonicalize_si UNSPEC. This preserves the ABI's modulo-32
pointer result even when the physical branch consumer observes 64 bits.
Apply to both ordinary and speculation-barrier relative tablejumps.
LP64, true 32-bit targets and absolute jump tables remain unchanged.
No Pmode, pointer layout, calling convention or SDK library changes.

--- a/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.md
+++ b/gcc/config/rs6000/rs6000.md
@@ -13377,6 +13377,17 @@
   rtx addr = gen_reg_rtx (Pmode);
 
   emit_insn (gen_add<mode>3 (addr, off, lab));
+  /* Pmode is SI in the Cell ELF64/ILP32 ABI, but add and mtctr use
+     all 64 GPR bits.  A negative relative offset loaded with lwz can
+     carry bit 32 into addr.  Preserve modulo-32 pointer arithmetic at
+     this control-flow consumer, using the same opaque canonicalization
+     as POINTER_PLUS_EXPR so combine cannot delete the truncation.  */
+  if (TARGET_64BIT && Pmode == SImode)
+    {
+      rtx canon = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
+      emit_insn (gen_ps3_ptr_canonicalize_si (canon, addr));
+      addr = canon;
+    }
   emit_jump_insn (gen_tablejump_insn_normal (Pmode, addr, operands[1]));
   DONE;
 })
@@ -13411,6 +13422,17 @@
   rtx addr = gen_reg_rtx (Pmode);
 
   emit_insn (gen_add<mode>3 (addr, off, lab));
+  /* Pmode is SI in the Cell ELF64/ILP32 ABI, but add and mtctr use
+     all 64 GPR bits.  A negative relative offset loaded with lwz can
+     carry bit 32 into addr.  Preserve modulo-32 pointer arithmetic at
+     this control-flow consumer, using the same opaque canonicalization
+     as POINTER_PLUS_EXPR so combine cannot delete the truncation.  */
+  if (TARGET_64BIT && Pmode == SImode)
+    {
+      rtx canon = gen_reg_rtx (SImode);
+      emit_insn (gen_ps3_ptr_canonicalize_si (canon, addr));
+      addr = canon;
+    }
   emit_jump_insn (gen_tablejump_insn_nospec (Pmode, addr, operands[1],
 					     operands[2]));
   DONE;
